1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,363
Welcome to Season 1! Three quick stories, then the cold hard facts: robot vacuums, space heaters and video doorbells.

2
00:00:06,713 --> 00:00:09,268
Episode 1. Sam really wants a robot vacuum.

3
00:00:09,418 --> 00:00:12,648
But I absolutely do not want a camera rolling in my house.

4
00:00:12,998 --> 00:00:14,956
Black Friday week. 11:48 p.m.

5
00:00:15,106 --> 00:00:18,802
Ooh, robot vacuums are on sale! Goodbye forever, dog hair!

6
00:00:19,152 --> 00:00:29,597
In 2022, photos taken by test robot vacuums were posted online, says MIT Technology Review. And in 2026, hacked robots showed live camera feeds, according to Tom's Hardware.

7
00:00:29,947 --> 00:00:32,550
Wait. My vacuum would have a CAMERA?

8
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:35,543
Yep! Many robots dodge your clutter by photographing it.

9
00:00:35,893 --> 00:00:38,742
But there's another way: a spinning laser called LiDAR.

10
00:00:38,892 --> 00:00:41,820
It measures distance. It never takes a photo.

11
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:44,685
It maps your home in the dark. No pictures.

12
00:00:45,035 --> 00:00:46,794
Then no camera, no problem!

13
00:00:46,944 --> 00:00:47,412
Mostly.

14
00:00:47,762 --> 00:00:51,566
Because it scans at the height of its turret, it easily sees the sofa, not the sock.

15
00:00:51,916 --> 00:01:05,530
In a CNET lab test from November 13, 2026, the camera-free Roomba 205 Combo avoided 1 of 6 hazards. But the Roomba Combo 10 Max with a camera avoided 6 of 6! Source is CNET, best robot vacuums of 2026, lab test by Ajay Kumar.

16
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:09,665
And no camera-free robot in our guide promises to avoid pet waste.

17
00:01:10,015 --> 00:01:12,961
BISCUIT IS A PUPPY! That's a dealbreaker!

18
00:01:13,311 --> 00:01:19,207
Which robot for your home? Tidy floor and privacy first? No camera. Puppy, sick pet, or cords? Camera robot.

19
00:01:19,557 --> 00:01:24,096
Next morning. Sam adopts the 30-second rule: cords and socks off the floor before every run.

20
00:01:24,246 --> 00:01:25,359
Floor's clear, buddy. Let's go.

21
00:01:25,709 --> 00:01:31,053
One more thing: a laser robot still sends your floor map to the cloud. Skip the data-sharing program in the app.

22
00:01:31,203 --> 00:01:32,513
No photos. Just us.

23
00:01:32,863 --> 00:01:40,991
Let's review! LiDAR is a spinning laser that measures distance and works in the dark. It scans at turret height to see the sofa, not the sock.

24
00:01:41,141 --> 00:01:50,155
Structured light reads an infrared pattern, and 'no RGB camera' is the accurate claim. Source: Maker product and support pages from November 23, 2026, and RTINGS.

25
00:01:50,505 --> 00:02:01,589
Without a camera, things get messy. 7 of 8 robots run into or drag cords. 4 of 8 eat socks, get stuck on rugs or tassels, or have navigation or docking errors.

26
00:02:01,739 --> 00:02:09,512
And 2 of 8 ran over pet waste in a test! Source: our reading of RTINGS, TechGearLab, T3, Tom's Guide, Best Buy owners and the TP-Link forum.

27
00:02:09,862 --> 00:02:19,376
Every photo leak we found had a camera. Dec 2022, test Roomba photos posted online. Aug 2024, Ecovacs robots taken over by Bluetooth.

28
00:02:19,526 --> 00:02:36,331
Oct 2024, hijacked Ecovacs robots in US homes! Sept 2025, a Dreame camera switched on remotely. Feb 2026, about 7,000 DJI robots reachable. Source: MIT Technology Review, TechCrunch (DEF CON), ABC Australia, KISA (Korea), and Tom's Hardware.

29
00:02:36,681 --> 00:02:45,721
Which robot for your home? Best all-round, no camera is the Roborock Q10 S5+. Lowest price for a tidy floor is Roborock Q7 M5+.

30
00:02:45,871 --> 00:03:00,590
Test sites' budget pick is the Tapo RV30 Max Plus. Hard floors, no room for a dock? Roomba 205 DustCompactor. A dock that washes the mops? Deebot N30 Pro Omni. Puppy, sick pet, cords everywhere? Get a camera robot. Source: Our guide, with CNET, RTINGS, The Verge and PCMag.

31
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:04,558
Episode 2. The first snow. Grandma June says she's perfectly fine.

32
00:03:04,908 --> 00:03:08,154
The first snow of the year, and Jo's grandmother lives all alone.

33
00:03:08,504 --> 00:03:12,286
Oh, don't fuss, dear. I have my trusty old heater.

34
00:03:12,636 --> 00:03:16,015
Grandma... what exactly is that heater plugged into?

35
00:03:16,365 --> 00:03:20,435
According to the CPSC, never plug a space heater into an extension cord or a power strip!

36
00:03:20,785 --> 00:03:23,243
Right. You're getting a new one. Tonight.

37
00:03:23,593 --> 00:03:27,589
Good call, Jo! But make one quick check before you buy any heater this winter.

38
00:03:27,939 --> 00:03:30,942
Find the model number on the label, then look it up in the recall notice.

39
00:03:31,292 --> 00:03:46,949
The October 29, 2026 CPSC recall covers the Dreo DR-HSH015, black with a remote. Units in the US were about 338,800, with a fire and burn hazard. Source: CPSC notice 27-054. The Dreo in our review is a different model; check yours against the notice.

40
00:03:47,299 --> 00:03:49,813
You drove all this way in the snow?

41
00:03:49,963 --> 00:03:51,328
You're worth the trip, Grandma.

42
00:03:51,678 --> 00:03:56,471
Plug it straight into the wall, and keep it three feet clear of drapes, furniture, and bedding, says the CPSC.

43
00:03:56,821 --> 00:04:01,212
Set it near 68°F. Dreo says in Eco mode it stops heating once the room gets there.

44
00:04:01,562 --> 00:04:03,598
Ah, warm at last.

45
00:04:03,948 --> 00:04:08,699
And turn it off when you sleep or leave: the CPSC and NFPA both say so. Goodnight, Grandma.

46
00:04:09,049 --> 00:04:16,246
Is one 1500 W heater enough? It handles roughly 150 to 200 square feet. That's one room, not the house!

47
00:04:16,396 --> 00:04:26,782
One owner found a heater sold for 1,000 sq ft barely managed 500. Also, oscillation is the noisiest setting, says Consumer Reports, Oct 2025. Source: Our Dreo review; Consumer Reports.

48
00:04:27,132 --> 00:04:32,990
Six habits that matter! Plug straight into the wall. Give it 3 feet of clearance from drapes, furniture, and bedding.

49
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:42,947
Keep the thermostat about 68°F, use Eco mode for long sessions, turn it off to sleep or leave, and each season: unplug, cool, and dust the inlet! Source: CPSC, NFPA and Dreo's support pages.

50
00:04:43,297 --> 00:04:49,986
Recall check on October 29, 2026! Model: Dreo DR-HSH015, black with remote.

51
00:04:50,136 --> 00:04:59,953
Units in the US are about 338,800, with a fire and burn hazard. If yours matches, stop using it and follow the notice. Source: CPSC recall notice 27-054. The Dreo in our review is a different model.

52
00:05:00,303 --> 00:05:05,769
Buy, wait or skip? Buy if you need it for one room, a few hours, with a remote and thermostat.

53
00:05:05,919 --> 00:05:14,676
Wait for Walmart deals, which were $29.99 to $43.99 last winter, and skip heating a whole house! Source: our review and Walmart deal posts, Nov 2025 to Jan 2026.

54
00:05:15,026 --> 00:05:17,637
Episode 3. Grandma June can't see her porch.

55
00:05:17,987 --> 00:05:20,126
Grandma June's porch. Tuesday, 2:10 p.m.

56
00:05:20,476 --> 00:05:23,758
Was someone at the door? My old ears aren't what they used to be.

57
00:05:24,108 --> 00:05:26,262
Grandma, let's get you a video doorbell.

58
00:05:26,612 --> 00:05:29,893
The catch: many doorbells save video only if you pay for a plan.

59
00:05:30,243 --> 00:05:33,685
A Ring with no plan is a live camera, not a recorder.

60
00:05:33,835 --> 00:05:37,893
Saved video costs extra: Ring Solo is $49.99 a year, says ring.com.

61
00:05:38,243 --> 00:05:50,843
What it costs over three years: eufy E340, no plan needed, is $119.99. Ring with the Solo plan is $189.96. Nest with Premium is $499.99. Ring with the Pro plan is $639.96.

62
00:05:50,993 --> 00:05:56,815
That's the doorbell price plus three years of plan fees, from our guide below, using Target and maker prices from November 11, 2026.

63
00:05:57,165 --> 00:06:02,248
$639.96 to watch Grandma's porch?! No way.

64
00:06:02,598 --> 00:06:08,213
Instead, eufy says the eufy E340 saves about 90 days of clips on 8 GB inside it. No fee.

65
00:06:08,563 --> 00:06:11,903
Look at you, my little engineer.

66
00:06:12,253 --> 00:06:15,369
Wow, I can see the whole porch!

67
00:06:15,719 --> 00:06:21,187
The catch with every battery doorbell: at a busy door, owners get weeks of charge, not months.

68
00:06:21,337 --> 00:06:23,598
Don't worry, I'll charge it on Sundays, when I visit.

69
00:06:23,948 --> 00:06:26,974
Ding dong! I know exactly who that is.

70
00:06:27,324 --> 00:06:32,597
Let's recap a Ring with no plan. Live view, two-way talk, and motion alerts are free.

71
00:06:32,747 --> 00:06:38,323
But saved video and person alerts? Plan needed. Source: ring.com; Ring Solo is $49.99 a year.

72
00:06:38,673 --> 00:06:53,238
Three-year cost! eufy E340, no plan, is $119.99. Tapo D225 plus microSD is $130 to $160. Reolink PoE plus microSD is $150 to $180.

73
00:06:53,388 --> 00:07:06,506
Aqara G410 plus microSD is $175 to $205. Ring plus Solo plan is $189.96. Nest plus Premium is $499.99, and Ring plus Pro plan is $639.96. Source: Target and maker prices, November 11, 2026.

74
00:07:06,856 --> 00:07:18,132
Pick by your home! For recordings, no plan, no card, get the eufy E340. For Home Assistant or a Reolink NVR, the Reolink PoE. iPhone and Apple Home? Aqara G410.

75
00:07:18,282 --> 00:07:27,320
Lowest cost with a card is Tapo D225. If you already pay for Ring, get the Ring Battery 2K, and for a Google home, the Nest Doorbell. Source: Our guide; PCMag, TechRadar, the makers.

76
00:07:27,670 --> 00:07:36,251
The battery catch! At busy doors, owners get weeks, not months. 'Wired' mode on eufy, Ring and Aqara battery models only trickle-charges.

77
00:07:36,401 --> 00:07:42,412
Fixes include a closer WiFi point, wiring, or a 16 V or larger transformer. Source: Owner reports collected in our guide.

78
00:07:42,762 --> 00:07:45,141
Every number in this video has a source.

79
00:07:45,291 --> 00:07:47,737
Read the full guides! Links to the full guides are in the description.

